# Build output and installed packages. Scoped to this directory rather than
# added to the root ignore file so the second implementation carries its own
# hygiene with it, the way the Rust workspace's `target/` rule does not have to
# know about Node.
dist/
node_modules/

# No lockfile is committed, and that is deliberate rather than an oversight:
# the only dependency in the tree is the TypeScript compiler, at dev time, and
# a lockfile would be a durable-looking record of a dependency graph this
# package's whole claim is that it does not have. CI installs with `npm
# install` and asserts the runtime-dependency list is empty.
package-lock.json
